@startuml student-transformation
title Use: make student data comparable to experience-oriented JDs (v2 — the bridge)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #C8E6C9
  BorderColor #2E7D32
}

start
:Student profile + evidence\n(projects, thesis, courses, internships, extracurriculars);

partition "1. Evidence normalization" {
  :Map each artifact to the SHARED competency vocabulary\n(same taxonomy nodes the JDs use);
  note right
    "Built a React app for my bachelor thesis"
      -> skills: React, frontend, REST
      -> evidence: project delivery
      -> provenance: THESIS / ACADEMIC_PROJECT
      -> confidence: medium (has GitHub link)
  end note
  :Attach provenance + confidence to every skill claim;
}

partition "2. Potential / readiness model (replaces years-of-experience)" {
  :Demonstrated skill depth\n(project complexity, did they ship?);
  :Learning velocity\n(self-taught stacks, breadth gained per semester);
  :Foundation quality\n(degree relevance to target domain);
  :Trajectory / initiative\n(hackathons, open-source, side projects);
  :-> potentialScore + learningSignals\n(maps to an entry/junior band, with a high-potential flag);
}

partition "3. JD reframing (meet the job halfway)" {
  :Use precomputed JobEntryProfile (diagram 05);
  :Compare against reinterpreted musts\n("3y React" -> "React foundation");
  :Split gaps into prerequisite vs learnable;
}

partition "4. Missing data & uncertainty" {
  if (Field captured?) then (yes)
    :use value + its confidence;
  else (no)
    :impute conservatively, FLAG as assumed;
    note right
      Distinguish:
      * evidence of absence (asked, none) -> real gap
      * absence of evidence (not captured) -> widen band,
        do NOT score as zero
    end note
  endif
  :Propagate confidence -> match score becomes a BAND,
   not a single point;
}

partition "5. Semantic bridge" {
  :Compare normalized competency profile to role\nin embedding space + LLM judgement\n(not raw CV-text vs JD-text keyword overlap);
}

:Comparable student representation\n(skills+provenance, potential, confidence-banded);
note right
  Net effect: student artifacts are translated into the
  same units the matching engine already speaks, the JD is
  translated down to entry terms, and the residual gap is
  expressed as honest uncertainty instead of fake zeros.
end note
stop
@enduml
